{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_25hqYtXlqy33qA5VNhHK4WYi","content":"1\t# Literature host interfaces · plan r5\n2\t\n3\t**Status: r5 draft, 2026-11-23. Not approved; r5's own bytes are not\n4\treviewed.** r5 answers the full GND review panel, which the owner selected\n5\t(D14, ruled `(o)`) and which ran over r4 (sha256\n6\t`6cadaa9134585b348d53ef50ef5c35638a3b0bb20c7c36726ac53039ac357cb6`): four of\n7\tsix reviewers succeeded, all asking for revision, with two blocking concerns\n8\tand twelve ranked fixes\n9\t([panel record](../../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/README.md)).\n10\tEach fix is applied and tagged `(p1)` at its sites; §11 maps every fix to\n11\tthem. The owner's rulings on D6, D9 and D10 (2026-11-22, r3) and on D14 and\n12\tD17 (2026-11-23, r4 and r5) are tagged `(o)`. r2 to r4 were never committed.\n13\tNo plan-gate record exists. The owner gates the plan before any spec is\n14\tapproved and before any code.\n15\t\n16\tThis plan covers [#216](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/216)\n17\tand [#215](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/215). It delivers\n18\tthe interface half of the \"host-scale reading and extraction\" carryover from\n19\tthe [literature-depth close](../../literature-depth/016-milestone-close.md).\n20\tThe run over a separately selected corpus and provider budget stays carried\n21\twith the literature-identity follow-up, as that close assigned it.\n22\t\n23\t**Provenance.** Outline r1 is the previous bytes of this file (sha256\n24\t`abefb05f7fa7c19d068182eeeb557efea36bbc89d555647d98ec350b1017bea0`, commit\n25\t`0cf94434`, merged in PR 219). Its phase IDs LH1–LH4 and decisions D1–D3 are\n26\tkept. Its reviews, `.gnd-planning/reviews/pr-219-r2/` and `pr-219-panel/`,\n27\tread the roadmap outline, not these bytes. The r4 panel's opinion covers r4's\n28\tbytes only; no sentence new in r5 carries a review opinion. Every code\n29\tcitation was re-read on 2026-11-22 at `4ad0d216`, and those r5 adds or\n30\tcorrects on 2026-11-23 at the same commit;\n31\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/` is unchanged since `0f39c392`, where the outline\n32\tcited it. The outline wrote the two module paths without `src/gnd/`; they are\n33\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/reading.py` and\n34\t`src/gnd/examples/literature/assertion_admission.py`. Below, `reading.py`,\n35\t`assertion_admission.py` and `depth.py` mean the files in that folder.\n36\t\n37\t## Goal and completion predicates\n38\t\n39\tA host with its own corpus and its own model calls the two literature examples\n40\tas library functions instead of reimplementing them. The examples stay\n41\texamples: neither is promoted to stable CLI (both issues say so).\n42\t\n43\t- **LH1.** `reading.py` has a public producer protocol. `run()` drives the six\n44\t  stages with a caller's producer over a caller's input root: its own\n45\t  documents, its own reading model with its own includes, no saved responses\n46\t  and no producer pin. Each of the fixture-only steps runs on caller data or\n47\t  is recorded as skipped. The run has a byte budget per document as well as\n48\t  the global one, and its caps are parameters. The responses and review\n49\t  receipts a live run produces are retained in its run folder.\n50\t- **LH2.** `replay()` re-derives a live LH1 run from its run folder and the\n51\t  caller's input root with zero producer calls and zero reviewer calls. It\n52\t  takes every setting from the run, and refuses a changed response, receipt or\n53\t  input.\n54\t- **LH3.** `assertion_admission.py` admits assertions of a caller-named entity\n55\t  in a caller's model. An assertion is identified by its own handle `(o)`.\n56\t  Every fact row attached to an admitted assertion is kept, whatever its fact\n57\t  type, together with the facts of the entities reached from it `(o)`. Absent\n58\t  optional facts are simply absent. An include root is admitted.\n59\t- **LH4.** Which values make a supported assertion admissible is caller data.\n60\t  A supported assertion that fails those rules has a status of its own. The\n61\t  target cap is a parameter.\n62\t\n63\tThe milestone is closed when each phase has its record and the close record\n64\tcites green focused lanes for LH1–LH4, the structure and inventory guards,\n65\tthe whole-repository `uv run ruff check`, as `project.md` requires `(p1)`,\n66\tthe replies drafted for #216 and #215, and the close review. Baseline, measured 2026-11-22 at `4ad0d216`\n67\twith gnd 0.4.0:\n68\t`uv run pytest -q tests/test_ld3_reading_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py\n69\ttests/test_ld5_verdict.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py\n70\t--tb=short` gave `90 passed in 166.21s`; `uv run ruff check src tests tools`\n71\texits 0. The whole-repository `uv run ruff check` exited 1 at `4ad0d216`,\n72\twith all 198 findings in the scripts delivered from dev-tools (H25). The owner\n73\thad them fixed upstream: dev-tools PR 34, merged as `a29562a`. After\n74\t`devtools/sync.py apply` from that commit, the whole-repository lint exits 0\n75\tand the gate-guard and scaffold tests pass (measured 2026-11-23). The re-sync\n76\tis committed with this plan, so LH1 starts from a `main` where the whole\n77\trepository lints clean `(p1)`.\n78\t\n79\t## 0. Binding design rules\n80\t\n81\t- **R0.1 Formats stay.** The stage record (`stage-N.json`), the attempt rows\n82\t  and their three outcomes, and the coverage rows with their eight states are\n83\t  unchanged; #216 says they work as they are. `literature-rebind/1` belongs to\n84\t  `interop.py` and is not touched.\n85\t- **R0.2 Packaged bytes stay.** With no new argument, the three packaged\n86\t  reading run configurations (`full`, `--scenario unavailable` and\n87\t  `--budget-bytes 0`; `SCENARIOS` itself has two values, `reading.py:38`)\n88\t  `(p1)` and the packaged admission write the bytes they write today. The comparison goes through `tests/support/recorded_version.py`,\n89\t  because the reading run retains two fidelity reports that carry\n90\t  `gnd_version` (H11).\n91\t- **R0.3 Example status stays.** Public here means named in the example's\n92\t  README and covered by tests. No `gnd` subcommand is added, and the two\n93\t  module command lines keep every argument they have.\n94\t- **R0.4 One loop, one walk.** Reading: the caller route and the packaged\n95\t  route run the same stage loop; the packaged constants become default data\n96\t  for it, not a second copy of it (standing rule 4). Admission `(p1)`: the\n97\t  D10 ruling keeps the packaged model, whose `assertion` objectifies a fact\n98\t  type, out of the generic projection, so admission has two projections, the\n99\t  packaged one as it is today and the generic attached-and-followed one. They\n100\t  share everything else, each in one home: the snapshot and the\n101\t  `gnd judgments check` route (`_judgments`, `_verify_report_inputs`), the\n102\t  mapping from a target's verdicts to a support reason (the target half of\n103\t  `_support`), the admission-rule evaluator of LH4, and the record writer and\n104\t  publication. The packaged projection gains no feature of the generic one;\n105\t  it stops at the packaged shape, as it does today.\n106\t- **R0.5 A setting is retained evidence.** Every argument that shapes a caller\n107\t  run is written into the run. Replay reads settings from the run, never from\n108\t  its caller.\n109\t- **R0.6 Skipped is not passed.** A step the caller did not supply is recorded\n110\t  with the status `skipped`. No report presents it as qualified, as measured\n111\t  or as zero.\n112\t- **R0.7 The stable commands stay the judges.** `gnd extract`, `verify`,\n113\t  `check`, `fidelity` and `judgments check` are invoked as today. Neither\n114\t  example re-implements one of their checks or widens one of their caps.\n115\t- **R0.8 A parameter has a ceiling.** Each cap that becomes a parameter has a\n116\t  hard maximum fixed in its spec, and a time-bound test at that maximum\n117\t  (standing rule 2).\n118\t\n119\tThe project's six standing rules\n120\t(`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`) bind every phase; each\n121\tspec discharges them by name.\n122\t\n123\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n124\t\n125\tHarvested obligations. \"Observed\" means re-read or run on 2026-11-22 at\n126\t`4ad0d216`; \"inherited\" means claimed by a source and not re-measured;\n127\t\"proposed\" means new in this plan.\n128\t\n129\t| # | Source | Obligation | Kind | Phase |\n130\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n131\t| H1 | #216 \"Problem\" | `run()` (`reading.py:562`) builds `SavedProducer(inputs.responses)` at `:566`; only the private `_evaluate(..., producer=)` at `:445` takes another | observed | LH1 |\n132\t| H2 | `reading.py`, `ReadingInputs` | the root is bound to saved responses by the pin (`:72-75`, \"saved producer table differs from its pin\") and by the roster check (`:113`, \"saved response roster differs\"), and to the packaged vocabulary (`:135`) | observed | LH1 |\n133\t| H3 | `reading.py`, stage loop | the fixture bindings: the outline's six, the producer label and, found by the panel, the calibration path's literals `(p1)`: the `unavailable` scenario names `study-methods` (`:448`); `_calibrate` names that section, the fact `approximation` (`:317`) and `CALIBRATION_FACTS` (`:42`, `:311-327`), and the absence floor is the literal `[2, 2]` (`:372`); and the calibration path also fixes its renderer label `authored-public-fixture` (`:300`), its case folders `run-methods` and `held-back-predicate` (`:320`, `:323`) and its count of two cases (`:335`) `(p1)`; `_combined` adds `LABEL` to every population (`:48`, `:247`); `_public_results` needs `conflict.json`, `conflict.txt`, a `subject_label` fact with exactly two labels and exits 1 from `verify` and `check` (`:395-407`); `absence_status` needs the predicate `alternative_integrator` (`:373`); `_review_attempts` needs a `reviews.json` receipt bound to each accepted response's facts digest 