ucer that raises refuses, naming the stage and section. **LH1-C9** the three packaged run configurations equal the trees recorded at `4ad0d216`, through the version helper `(p1)`; `test_ld3`, `test_ld4` and `test_ld5` pass unedited. **LH1-C10** each limit at its ceiling stays within the spec's time bound: inputs at each roster ceiling load, with the input cap raised as they need; a source at the input-cap ceiling, a response at the response-cap ceiling and a budget at its ceiling each run; a route that reaches the timeout refuses within the timeout plus its grace. The spec may let ceilings share one test if it says which and why `(p1)`. **LH1-C11** a model `gnd extract` refuses, and a live producer over a root with no profile, each refuse before any producer call. **LH1-C12** `replay()` of a `/2` run exits 3. **LH1-C13** a caller run whose broad population leaves a constrained fact type empty completes and records exit 2 for it; one whose targeted population violates a constraint completes and records exit 1; exit 4 is recorded like 2, held by a caller model whose check exits 4 or, if the spec shows no caller model can reach it, by a unit test of the exit table `(p1)`. **LH1-C14** `(p1)` a run whose retained-file bound exceeds the retained-file cap refuses before any producer call; a run at the response and roster ceilings, with the retained-file cap raised to fit, completes | H20 stays carried |\n371\t| LH2 | **LH2-C1** the LH1-C1 run replays from its folder and the caller root, byte-identical, with the same evidence digest and zero calls. **LH2-C2** one changed byte in the response table or in a receipt refuses; a consistently rewritten folder refuses when the expected digest is given. **LH2-C3** a run recorded with non-default limits replays with them, including the LH1-C14 run at the response and roster ceilings `(p1)`; a manifest with a setting above its ceiling refuses. **LH2-C4** a changed source, profile, model or include refuses \"stale reading input\". **LH2-C5** a `/1` run replays as today; `test_ld3`, `test_ld4`, `test_ld5` pass unedited. **LH2-C6** `score_reading_coverage` scores the caller run when given its root. **LH2-C7** a manifest that claims `skipped` for a step the profile declares refuses | none |\n372\t| LH3 | **LH3-C1** a model with claims that share a passage, a claim with two actors and no object, one with three conditions and one with a quantity that is an entity with a value row and a unit row `(o)` admits; every attached row of each admitted claim is kept, with the rows of its quantity `(o)`, and no row of another claim is; `gnd check` on the admitted population exits 0. **LH3-C2** `(o)` a shape naming an entity that objectifies a fact type, the packaged `assertion` for one, exits 3 with a reason that names the objectification, and nothing is published. **LH3-C3** a claim with one admitted and one rejected target is not admitted; a claim with one admitted target and untargeted rows is, with all its rows; a claim with no target has disposition `missing`. **LH3-C4** a row between two assertions is kept only when both are admitted. **LH3-C5** the model as an include root admits and the record binds each include; an include edited without a new pin exits 3 with nothing published. **LH3-C6** each refusal in the spec's list exits 3 with a value-free reason and nothing published. **LH3-C7** the value `none` in a generic-shape row is an ordinary value. **LH3-C8** the packaged call writes `admitted.population.json` and `raw.population.json` with the H18 digests and the H18 stage table; `test_li4` and `test_li5` pass unedited. **LH3-C9** 1,024 targets with attached and followed rows up to the `max_rows` ceiling project within the spec's time bound; one row over `max_rows` refuses `(p1)`. **LH3-C10** `(o)` a quantity named by an admitted and by a rejected claim keeps its own rows once, and the rejected claim's row that names it is not kept; a row reached through a followed entity that names a rejected claim is not kept; an entity type the shape does not list is not followed (D17) | H15 closes here |\n373\t| LH4 | **LH4-C1** two rules files over the same inputs admit two different sets, each stated in the fixture. **LH4-C2** a supported assertion that fails a requirement has status `policy-refused`; an unsupported one has `fail`. **LH4-C3** an assertion with one admissible and one inadmissible row of the named fact type is `policy-refused`; so is one with no row of it. **LH4-C4** a lowered `max_targets` refuses a policy over it; a value above 1,024 refuses the call. **LH4-C5** a requirement naming an unknown fact type or role, and each malformed rules document in the spec's list, exit 3 with nothing published. **LH4-C6** the packaged call keeps the H18 bytes and statuses, now through the default rules and the one evaluator `(p1)`. **LH4-C7** `(p1)` a `/2` record binds the shape and rules digests and records `max_targets` and `max_rows`; changing any one changes the record; a call with rules and no shape writes `/2` with the shape `packaged` | none |\n374\t\n375\tEach phase also runs the structure and inventory guards, the\n376\twhole-repository `uv run ruff check` `(p1)`, an independent review of its\n377\tdiff, a refactoring review and its record.\n378\t\n379\t## 5. Documentation, skill and compatibility surfaces\n380\t\n381\t- **One home each.** The reading protocol, the profile, the limits and the\n382\t  `/2` manifest are described in\n383\t  `src/gnd/examples/literature/reading_fixture/README.md`, which already\n384\t  holds the stage files and the coverage states. The assertion shape, the\n385\t  admission rules and the `/2` record are described in the admission section\n386\t  of `src/gnd/examples/literature/README.md`. `docs/literature/commands.md`\n387\t  gains one short \"drive it from your host\" passage per example that links to\n388\t  those two homes and restates nothing normative.\n389\t- **Release notes.** One entry per pair under the unreleased heading of\n390\t  `docs/release-notes.md`, written by LH2 and LH4.\n391\t- **Skills.** No packaged skill names these functions; none changes.\n392\t- **Compatibility.** `SavedProducer.produce` takes one call object where it\n393\t  took two names; `test_ld3` patches it with a function that accepts any\n394\t  arguments. `test_ld3` also calls `_inspect` directly with six positional\n395\t  arguments and reads `SavedProducer.calls`, and patches `reading._read` on\n396\t  the replay path (H10). These stay: `_inspect` keeps its six positional\n397\t  parameters and its return shape, and every new parameter is keyword-only;\n398\t  `SavedProducer` keeps its `calls` counter, though the loop no longer needs\n399\t  one; `reading._read` stays the replay read path `(p1)`. `run()`, `replay()`, `admit()` and\n400\t  `project()` keep their present arguments and defaults. `/1` readers are not\n401\t  given `/2` documents by any packaged route.\n402\t- **Issue replies.** The close drafts a reply to #216 and to #215. Each says\n403\t  what was not done: the 1,024-target ceiling (H13), the corpus run (H20) and\n404\t  admission of an objectified fact type (D10).\n405\t  The owner posts them.\n406\t\n407\t## 6. Risks and required controls\n408\t\n409\t| Risk | Control |\n410\t|---|---|\n411\t| The generic projection admits rows the packaged example refused | LH3-C8 and LH4-C6 pin the packaged admitted set, the stage table and the output digests |\n412\t| Dropping the saved-response pin for live runs weakens the packaged replay | the pin and roster checks stay for `SavedProducer` (existing `test_ld3` cases); LH2-C2 binds a live run by digest |\n413\t| A caller root silently gets a packaged constant | the profile is the only source of caller bindings; LH1-C1 searches the run folder for packaged names |\n414\t| A skipped step reads as a passed one | R0.6; LH1-C4 and LH2-C7 |\n415\t| A provider answer crashes the loop after spend | LH1-C7, LH1-C8; the order rule and LH1-C11 put every input and model refusal before the first call |\n416\t| A completed caller run is read as a verified extraction | D16; the report carries the route exits, the README says a completed run is not a verified one, and LH1-C13 holds a run that completes with exits 2 and 1 |\n417\t| Following outward keeps a rejected assertion's row, or grows to most of the population | the limit in §2 \"Followed facts\" and D17; LH3-C10 holds a shared entity, a row reached the long way round and an unlisted entity type |\n418\t| The reporter's assertion is an objectified fact type after all | LH3-C2 refuses it by name, and the #215 reply states the ruling (D10), so the mismatch is reported, not silent |\n419\t| A raised cap turns a legal input into minutes of CPU | R0.8; LH1-C10, LH3-C9 |\n420\t| A live run retains files that its own replay cannot read `(p1)` | the retained-file cap is recorded, `run()` bounds its files before the first call; LH1-C14, LH2-C3 |\n421\t| The generic admission path drifts from the packaged one `(p1)` | R0.4 names the shared homes; LH4-C6 runs the packaged rules through the one evaluator |\n422\t| A rule quantified \"any\" or \"every\" passes on fixtures that cannot tell them apart | LH3-C3, LH3-C4 and LH4-C3 each hold the discriminating case |\n423\t| A host reads \"parameter\" as \"no limit\" for `MAX_TARGETS` | LH4-C4; the README and the #215 reply state the stable ceiling |\n424\t| A large caller vocabulary exceeds the route timeout ([#221](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/221)) | the timeout is a limit (D4); a route that times out refuses naming the route |\n425\t| LH1 is larger than one phase | its spec states the size; if the estimate passes 400 source lines the spec proposes a split at its gate, with new IDs LH1a and LH1b |\n426\t| The packaged bytes pin moves at a version bump | the comparison uses `tests/support/recorded_version.py`, with `RECORDED_AT = \"0.4.0\"` |\n427\t\n428\t## 7. Out of scope\n429\t\n430\tThe corpus and provider-budget run