g_workflow.py tests/test_ld4_revision.py tests/test_ld5_verdict.py tests/test_li1_assurance_report.py --tb=short`, then `uv run python tools/run_tutorials.py --group literature` | exit 0 each |\n462\t| LH3 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py --tb=short` | exit 0 |\n463\t| LH4 | `uv run pytest -q tests/test_lh4_admission_rules.py tests/test_lh3_admission_shape.py tests/test_li4_assertions.py tests/test_li5_lineage.py --tb=short`, then `uv run python tools/run_tutorials.py --group literature` | exit 0 each |\n464\t| all | the structure and inventory guard block of `project.md`, and the whole-repository `uv run ruff check` `(p1)` | exit 0 |\n465\t\n466\tAffected consumers named here are read at each spec and may be widened there.\n467\tNo broad lane (`-m \"evidence or census\"`) is selected.\n468\t\n469\t## 10. Owner decisions and open questions\n470\t\n471\tD6, D9 and D10 carry the owner's ruling of 2026-11-22 `(o)`, and D14 and D17\n472\tthe rulings of 2026-11-23 `(o)`. Every other row is a proposal until the plan\n473\tgate rules it. D1–D3 keep their outline IDs; D4–D16 are new in r2, D17 in r3\n474\tand D18 in r5.\n475\t\n476\t| ID | Question | Proposed | What the other reading costs |\n477\t|---|---|---|---|\n478\t| D1 | Where the producer protocol lives | In `reading.py`, until a second example uses it | A shared module now is a public home with one user |\n479\t| D2 | Name and reach of the LH4 disposition | `policy-refused`, in the `/2` record only; `/1` keeps `fail` | Applying it to `/1` changes the packaged record's bytes and `test_li4`'s expectations |\n480\t| D3 | The fixture-only steps on a caller root | Calibration, the conflict check and the absence scope are optional and declared in the profile; an undeclared step is `skipped`. The population label is profile data. A reviewer is optional, and a decision other than `supported` refuses the run | A reviewer that filters instead needs a ninth coverage state, which changes the row format #216 asks to keep |\n481\t| D4 | Which caps become parameters, and their ceilings | Seven limits `(p1)`: roster cap (default 128, ceiling 4,096), largest budget (1 MiB, 64 MiB), per-file input (128 KiB, 8 MiB), response (128 KiB, today's effective bound, since a response cannot exceed the 128 KiB read of `responses.json`; ceiling 1 MiB), route timeout (30 s, 600 s), route output (1 MiB, 16 MiB), retained file (128 KiB, today's read of a run's own files; ceiling 64 MiB). A JSON file is decoded under its read cap. `document_budget` is a `run()` argument whose ceiling is the largest-budget limit | #216 names the first two only; with only those, a source over 128 KiB still refuses, a slow `gnd check` still stops the run at 30 s, and a live run can retain files its replay cannot read (H5) |\n482\t| D5 | Manifest format of a caller run | `literature-reading-run/2` for any run that uses a new argument; `/1` unchanged otherwise | Optional keys in `/1` let an older reader accept a run it cannot re-derive |\n483\t| D6 | What \"the stop rule per document\" means | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-22: as proposed.** A byte budget per source, enforced in the loop, and a stop reason per source in the report. A document whose required questions are resolved still gets its other scheduled reads | Ending a document at required coverage reads less, and changes which optional questions are answered; it could be a later switch |\n484\t| D7 | A malformed response, or a producer that raises | Refuse the run with nothing written; a host that prefers to continue returns `refused` from its own producer | Recording it as `refused` reports a transport failure as the producer's verdict |\n485\t| D8 | LH3: what is judged, and how row verdicts make an assertion's verdict | Targets are attached rows; supported means at least one target and every target admitted | \"Any target admitted\" admits an assertion with a rejected participant row |\n486\t| D9 | LH3: how far \"hangs off\" reaches | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-22: the other reading, follow entities outward.** Not adopted: directly attached fact types only; they form `covers`; other fact types are not copied | Following entities outward keeps a quantity entity's own facts, at the price of a reachability rule the model does not state. That rule is D17 |\n487\t| D10 | LH3: linking an objectified fact's row to its handle | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-22: the other reading, own handle only.** Not adopted: a link through the preferred external uniqueness, each identifying role matched to a role of the same name and object type in the objectified fact type | No rule means the objectified form is refused and only entities with their own handle are admitted, which leaves the packaged model on the old path only |\n488\t| D11 | LH4: the ceiling of `max_targets` | 1,024, the stable command's cap; a larger set is admitted in several calls the host makes | Raising `judgments.py`'s caps changes a stable command; that would be its own issue |\n489\t| D12 | LH3: the record of a shaped call | `literature-assertion-admission/2`; the packaged call keeps `/1` | One format with optional keys makes `lineage_run.py:254` accept records it was not written for |\n490\t| D13 | Phase diff reviewer | The review helper (`.claude/skills/process-phase/scripts/review_tool.py`, subject `phase`), one reviewer in a different tool | none; this is `project.md`'s default |\n491\t| D14 | Plan-review instrument | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-23: the full GND panel** (\"full\"). Its first round read r4; a second round over r5 is the owner's call | none |\n492\t| D15 | How the milestone runs | The owner selects: phase by phase with an owner gate on each spec, or `process-milestone … auto` | none |\n493\t| D16 | LH1: which `verify` and `check` exits let a caller run complete | 0, 1, 2 and 4 are recorded and the run completes; the host gates on them; any other exit refuses (H24) `(p1)` | Requiring 0, as the packaged root does, refuses every run over a model with a constraint on a fact type not yet read (H23). Refusing on 1 only loses every producer call of a run whose extraction violates a constraint, which is a finding the host wants kept |\n494\t| D17 | LH3: where following stops (opened by the D9 ruling) | **Ruled `(o)` 2026-11-23: as proposed.** The shape lists the entity types to follow, for example `quantity`; an instance of any other entity type is kept as a value in the row that names it, and its own facts are not copied | Not adopted: following every entity type. It needs no list, but one admitted claim then keeps its paper, the paper's authors, their other papers and so on: most of the population, whatever was judged. With an empty list the result is the reading D9 did not adopt |\n495\t| D18 | LH3: the generic projection's row bound `(p1)` | A `max_rows` argument, default 16,384, ceiling 65,536, bounding attached and followed rows together; separate from `max_targets`. The packaged projection keeps `MAX_TARGETS` as its row bound | Reusing `max_targets` as the row bound refuses 1,024 claims with two actors each (H19) |\n496\t\n497\tThe owner ruled D6, D9, D10 and D17 without waiting for the reporter. The\n498\treply to #215 states the three LH3 rulings, so the reporter can say if their\n499\tmodel does not fit them: an assertion is identified by its own handle,\n500\tadmission follows outward from it, and the host lists the entity types it\n501\tfollows.\n502\t\n503\t## 11. Rulings before the gate\n504\t\n505\t### 2026-11-22, r3\n506\t\n507\tOwner rulings given in the planning session, in reply to the three questions\n508\tr2 marked for the reporter. The owner's words: \"d6: proposed\", \"d9:\n509\talternative\", \"d10: own number\". Prior wording is r2's.\n510\t\n511\t| Tag | Site | Prior wording (r2) | Now |\n512\t|---|---|---|---|\n513\t| o | §10 D6; §2 LH1 \"Per document\" | proposal, \"To confirm with the reporter\" | ruled as proposed; no criterion changes |\n514\t| o | §10 D9; Goal LH3; §2 LH3 \"Attached facts\" | \"The admitted population holds exactly the attached rows of admitted assertions, and its `covers` lists the attached fact types (D9).\" | \"Followed facts\" and \"Coverage\" in §2; LH3-C1 widened; LH3-C10 added; D17 opened |\n515\t| o | §10 D10; Goal LH3; §2 LH3 \"Identity\" | \"For an entity that objectifies a fact type, a row of that fact type is linked to its handle through the entity's preferred external uniqueness, role by role (D10, H14). A row that links to no handle or to two refuses.\" | own handle only; an objectifying entity refuses under a shape |\n516\t| o | §4 LH3-C2 | \"the packaged model under a shape naming `assertion` admits exactly the statements whose target is admitted, each with its two link rows\" | the refusal of an objectifying entity |\n517\t| o | §7 | \"facts reachable from an assertion only through another entity (D9)\" | removed; two items added for D10 and D17 |\n518\t\n519\t### 2026-11-23, r4\n520\t\n521\tOwner ruling on D17, the question the D9 ruling opened. Asked \"the host lists\n522\tthe types, or follow everything?\", with the list as the proposal, the owner\n523\tanswered \"your auggestion\", read here as \"your suggestion\": the proposal.\n524\tPrior wording is r3's.\n525\t\n526\t| Tag | Site | Prior wording (r3) | Now |\n527\t|---|---|---|---|\n528\t| o | §10 D17 | proposal, with \"follow every entity type\" as the other reading | ruled as proposed |\n529\t| o | §2 LH3 \"Followed facts\" | \"Where the walk stops is D17. One limit holds under every reading of D17\" | the walk stops at the shape's list; an empty list follows nothing |\n530\t| o | §7 | \"following an entity type the shape does not list (D17, if ruled as proposed)\" | \"(D17, ruled)\" |\n531\t\n532\tNo criterion changed: LH3-C10 already holds an entity type the shape does not\n533\tlist.\n534\t\n535\t### 2026-11-23, r5: the panel's fixes\n536\t\n537\tThe full panel over r4 (D14) returned two blocking concerns and twelve ranked\n538\tfixes ([PANEL-REVIEW.md](../../../reviews/literature-host-interfaces-r4-panel/PANEL-REVIEW.md)).\n539\tEvery cited code fact was re-checked at `4ad0d216` before a fix was written,\n540\tand each held. Every fix is applied; sites are tagged `(p1)`.\n541\t\n542\t| Fix | Concern (reviewers) | Sites in r5 |\n543\t|---|---|---|\n544\t| 1 | R0.4 cannot hold for admission under the D10 ruling (Claude, blocking) | §0 R0.4 names the two projections and their shared homes; §2 LH4 \"Rules\" and \"Default rules\"; LH4-C6; §6 |\n545\t| 2 | the narrowed lint gate conflicts with `project.md` (Codex, blocking) | the owner had the dev-tools scripts fixed (dev-tools PR 34, `a29562a`) and gnd-public re-synced; the whole-repository lint is the gate in the completion predicates, §4 and §9; H25 |\n546\t| 3 | retained files can outgrow the fixed read caps (Claude) | H5; §2 LH1 \"Limits\" and \"Retained files\"; §2 LH2; D4; LH1-C14; LH2-C3; §6 |\n547\t| 4 | `gnd check` exit 4 is not covered (Claude) | H24; §2 LH1 \"Route exits\"; D16; LH1-C13 |\n548\t| 5 | the 64 KiB response default is not today's constant (Claude, Kimi, GLM) | D4: 128 KiB, today's effective bound |\n549\t| 6 | the per-document budget's semantics, home and ceiling, and the D6 continuation criterion (Claude, Kimi, GLM) | §2 LH1 \"Per document\"; D4; LH1-C5 |\n550\t| 7 | a time bound at every ceiling (Kimi) | LH1-C10 |\n551\t| 8 | the generic projection has no row bound (Claude) | §2 LH3 \"Row bound\"; D18 (new, proposed); LH3-C9 |\n552\t| 9 | the admission record does not bind its settings (Claude) | §2 LH3 \"Record\"; LH4-C7 |\n553\t| 10 | the unavailable scenario has no owner on a caller root (Claude) | §2 LH1 \"Unavailable sections\"; LH1-C4 |\n554\t| 11 | §5 misstates how `test_ld3` reaches the producer (Claude) | H10; §5 \"Compatibility\" |\n555\t| 12 | citations: H10 lines (Claude, GLM), H3 calibration literals (Claude), \"three scenarios\" (GLM) | H10; H3; §2 LH1 \"A caller root\"; R0.2; LH1-C9 |\n556\t\n557\tD14 is recorded as ruled: the owner answered \"full\" when asked which review\n558\tthe plan should get. Fix 2's direction is the owner's: asked how the plan\n559\tshould handle the lint gate, the owner answered \"fix the devtools script\n560\tfirst\", then \"merge pr 34\" and \"override and merge\"."}
